+## `bin/clean-workspaces.sh`
+
+Removes stale build workspaces: every immediate subdirectory of the workspace root whose
+newest file is more than the threshold number of days old. Symlinks are skipped, and a
+directory containing no files is aged by its own modification time. Requires GNU `find` and
+Bash 4.4 or later.
+
+```
+bin/clean-workspaces.sh [--root DIR] [--days N] [--dry-run]
+```
+
+| Option | Default | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `-r`, `--root DIR` | `workspaces` | Directory containing the workspaces (relative paths resolve from the current directory). |
+| `-d`, `--days N` | `7` | Remove workspaces older than `N` whole days. Must be a non-negative integer. |
+| `-n`, `--dry-run` | off | Print `would remove <name> (age <N>d)` for each candidate and remove nothing. |
+| `-h`, `--help` | | Show usage. |
+
+Examples:
+
+```
+bin/clean-workspaces.sh                                    # workspaces/, 7 days
+bin/clean-workspaces.sh --root /srv/ci/work --days 14
+bin/clean-workspaces.sh --root /srv/ci/work --dry-run      # preview first
+```
+
+Exit status: `0` on success, `64` for a usage error (bad option, non-numeric `--days`, or
+a root of `/`), `66` if the root is not an accessible directory.
